<title>MEXICO: Mexico Cetes rates fall across board in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico Cetes rates fall across board in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's benchmark 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	20.04	    -39	     19.98     20.08</p>
<p>91-Day	21.24	    -54	     21.24     21.24</p>
<p>182-Day     21.29	    -74	     21.18     21.42</p>
<p>350-Day     22.20				22.13     22.29</p>
<p>Last week the 357-day paper was assigned at 22.96 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	800 million pesos   2.92 bln pesos     3.65</p>
<p>91-Day	800 million pesos   4.23 bln pesos     5.29</p>
<p>182-Day     800 million pesos   2.95 bln pesos     3.69</p>
<p>350-Day     600 million pesos   2.20 bln pesos     3.67</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.1 on demand of 12.3 billion pesos compared with 4.53 the week before on demand of 13.6 billion pesos the week before. Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    4 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			    0 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  13 basis points</p>
<p>    350-Day			   9 basis points</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
